  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the fourth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-1}-5,\\,{a}_{1}=6,\\,n\\ge 2.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Starting with the first term ${a}_{1}=6,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fourth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =6 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2{a}_{1}-5=2\\cdot 6-5=7 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2{a}_{2}-5=2\\cdot 7-5=9 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2{a}_{3}-5=2\\cdot 9-5=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is ${a}_{4}=13.$",
